GAL22V10
UA6RH001

AB1 AB2 AB3 AB4 AB5 AB6 GALSTB RCFG8 RCFG4 RCFG2 BASEA GND
RW CFGIN NC15 ACPHASE RST DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12 NC22 DRVEN VCC

; =====================================================================
; UA6 - RocHard RH800C  -  ua6_hd + base latch -> (0,0,1)  (RAM bring-up)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; IDENTICAL to ua6_hd.pld (working HD, latched /_DRVEN) EXCEPT DB12 (p21)
; AND DB14 (p19) are driven LOW while reset is asserted. DB13 (p20) is
; left Hi-Z (natural 1).  Target base latch (o16,o17,o18)=(0,0,1) =
; (CFGD12,CFGD14,CFGD13)=(0,0,1).
;
; WHY (LA-derived + confirmed 2026-08-01):
;   The strap-on crash = UA4's /GALCLK1 (o19) arms a wrong-region term ->
;   /_GALSTROBE -> /_RAMCE -> U2 fights the bus at that region -> crash.
;   Which term arms depends ENTIRELY on the base latch o16/o17/o18:
;     base 111 -> line37 -> region 7 ($F8 Kickstart)   [orig red screen]
;     base 110 -> line36 -> $C0-$DF ($D8 CIA)          [ua6_hd_db13 yellow]
;     base 001 -> line35 -> $200000 (the 2M RAM window) [CORRECT]
;   Verified base=(0,0,1)+2M strap arms line35 ONLY (all 15 o19 terms
;   checked) -> /_GALSTROBE fires ONLY at $200000, nowhere spurious.
;
;   For 2M @ $200000, line35 = i6 & /i7 & /i8 (A21=1,A22=0,A23=0) &
;   i9 & i10 & /i11 (2M strap) & /o16 & /o17 & o18  => need o16=0, o17=0,
;   o18=1.  ua6_hd_db13 wrongly forced o18=0 (-> 110 -> $D8). This forces
;   o16=0 (DB12) + o17=0 (DB14) and leaves o18=1 (DB13 natural).
;
;   Mechanism (proven by ua6_hd_db13: CFGD13 held 0 all boot): UA4's
;   o16/o17/o18 latches release when /_DRVEN is high (reset); driving the
;   DB line low then makes UA4 capture 0 at reset-release and hold it.
;   Controller er_Type ($D1: DB12=1,DB14=1) stays correct because the ROM
;   drives DB12/DB14 strong during the $E8 read - the 32.7R resistors
;   decouple UA4's internal 0 from the bus the OS reads.
;
;   /_DRVEN UNCHANGED from ua6_hd -> HD autoconfig unaffected.
;
; NOTE: this points the RAM WINDOW at $200000; it does NOT yet make the OS
;   USE the RAM (announcement / AddMemList is separate). Goal here: stop
;   ALL spurious-region contention so the machine boots clean with the
;   strap on, and the RAM decodes where it belongs.
;
; BOARD: game II - DIP-1 ON - DIP-2 ON - JPA1 2M. SIMMs: out for the
;   clean-boot check, then in to look for $200000 (region 00100) access.
; =====================================================================


; ---- /_DRVEN (pin 23) : UNCHANGED working latched version -----------
/DRVEN = /CFGIN & /BASEA & RST
       + /CFGIN & /DRVEN & RST


; ---- /_AC_PHASE (pin 16) : Hi-Z (unchanged) -------------------------
ACPHASE.T = VCC
ACPHASE.E = AB1 & /AB1


; ---- DB15 (pin 18), DB13 (pin 20) : Hi-Z (natural 1 held by UA4) ----
DB15.T = VCC
DB15.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB13.T = VCC
DB13.E = AB1 & /AB1

; ---- DB12 (pin 21) + DB14 (pin 19) : drive LOW while RESET asserted -
; .T tautological-false -> data 0 -> pin LOW (active-high decl).
; .E = /RST -> only while reset asserted; Hi-Z after (ROM/UA4 own the
; line in normal ops; UA4 holds the captured 0 internally).
DB12.T = AB1 & /AB1
DB12.E = /RST
DB14.T = AB1 & /AB1
DB14.E = /RST


; ---- NC15 (pin 15), NC22 (pin 22) : Hi-Z (unchanged) ----------------
NC15.T = VCC
NC15.E = AB1 & /AB1
NC22.T = VCC
NC22.E = AB1 & /AB1


DESCRIPTION

UA6 HD build + base-latch->(0,0,1) for RocHard RH800C 2M RAM bring-up.

Same as ua6_hd.pld except DB12 (p21) and DB14 (p19) are driven LOW during
reset, so UA4 captures o16=0 and o17=0 (DB13/o18 left natural = 1). Base
latch (o16,o17,o18)=(0,0,1) arms ONLY UA4 /GALCLK1 line35 = the 2M
$200000 window; disarms the $F8 (line37) and $C0-$DF (line36) terms that
caused the red and yellow screens. Controller ID intact (ROM drives the
$E8 read; 32.7R decouples). /_DRVEN unchanged -> HD unaffected.

TEST (LA, roctec_ram_cfgd channel map):
  1. RAM off: HD still boots (must).
  2. RAM on, SIMMs out: does it boot CLEAN now (no red/yellow)? Does
     /_RAMCE / /_GALSTROBE stop firing at $F8 AND $D8? CFGD12/14/13 = 0,0,1?
  3. RAM on, SIMMs in bank0: any access at region 00100 ($200000)?
